-- title:
--   Node coordinates and chain position at one supersingular crossing
-- statement:
--   Setting. Fixed throughout are an integer $N_0 \neq 0$, a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$ (hypothesis `hqN`), a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`), and a ring homomorphism $\rho : R_q \to A$ whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map of $R_q$ (`hρ`). The residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField ↥A` is assumed of characteristic $q$ and algebraically closed, and the residue map $A \to \kappa$ is assumed surjective (`hred`). Further, $\mathfrak P$ is a Deligne–Rapoport model package at level $N_0q$, i.e. a term of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`: a proper, flat, integral model `X N₀ q` of the Igusa scheme over $\operatorname{Spec} R_q$, with all affine sections integrally closed, together with a curve model `Meta` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-curve with function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)`, an isomorphism `eeta` of it onto the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ compatible with the structure maps, Galois equivariance `hgal` of the induced identification of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points with places, a pinning `Meta_pin` of the finite Igusa chart functions to their $q$-expansions, smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre, sections `εinf`, `εzero`, and further data.
--
--   Arithmetic base. $O$ is a discrete valuation domain, `eO` an isomorphism of $O$ onto the valuation subring obtained by pulling $A$ back along the inclusion into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the fixed field of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$), `hϖO` says the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $q$, $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ satisfies the compatibility `hρO` that its composite with the embedding $O \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ determined by `eO` and the fixed field is the structure map of $R_q$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ is computed by `htoκ` as the residue map of $A$ applied to that embedding.
--
--   Characteristic-$q$ modular input. `data` is a `ModularPolynomialData q` (a monic bivariate $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating $j$, $j_q$), `hKr` the Kronecker congruence $\overline\Phi = (C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$, and `hα`, `hβ` the integrality of the Hecke maps $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$ at level $(N_0,q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. `fm` is a fibre model `CharPModel.FibreModel N₀ A q κ` for the residue map (two subrings `BFin`, `BInf` of the base change of the full modular function field, integral over the affine bases, with reduction homomorphisms to `modularFunctionFieldC κ N₀` and the usual normalisations on $j$, $j_{N_0}$), `cc` its cusp chart property ($\bar j_{N_0}\bar j^{-N_0} \in$ `BInf` with the expected reduction), and `hfin`, `hinf` state that the coefficient-embedded elements of the Igusa chart algebras `chartAlgFin N₀ q`, `chartAlgInf N₀ q` lie in `fm.BFin`, `fm.BInf` respectively. `dataAll` supplies modular polynomial data for every divisor of $N_0$ and `hsepΦ` the separability of $\Phi_{N_0}$ reduced modulo $q$, viewed in `RatFunc κ`.
--
--   Specialisation and prolongation. $P$ is a `PlaceSpecialization A q N₀ data hKr κ (residue A) hα hβ`, a bundle consisting of a map `sp` from places of `modularFunctionFieldBar N₀` to places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N₀`, a homomorphism on degree-zero divisor classes, and many compatibility clauses on orders of $j$, $j_{N_0}$ and cusps (summarised here); `hP` identifies `P.sp` with `fm.spPlace hred dataAll hsepΦ`. $R$ is a `ProlongationTuple P` (two regular prolongations $R_1$, $R_2$ of $A$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` with residue fields over $\kappa$, together with the reduction-compatibility clauses); `hR` asserts `R.IsModel`, the conjunction of the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws; `hO` asserts `R.OrderLawFixed`, the statement that for $f$ integral for both prolongations with non-zero residues, the pushforward along `P.reduceFst` of the divisor of $f$ at a Frobenius-fixed affine geometric place $v$ equals $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the first residue plus $\operatorname{ord}$ of the second residue at the Frobenius translate of $v$. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ N₀` which, by `hW`, is exactly the set `ssPlaces q N₀ κ` of supersingular places; `hreg` is `R.RegularityLaw W` and `hval` is `R.NodeValueLaw W` (the non-negativity clauses, and the clause producing a common non-zero residue value at a node pair). A function $e$ on places is given with `he`: $e(w) =$ `placeWidthChar q N₀ w` for $w \in W$, the width invariant $j$-width divided by the ramification index of $j$ at $w$. Finally `hVI` asserts `R.ValueIntegralityLaw w` for each $w \in W$: every $f$ in `R.nodeIntegers w` has $V$-value in $A$ for every place $V$ with `P.reduceFst V = w`.
--
--   The crossing and its chart presentation. The fibre `DRLevel.fibre0` over $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ is assumed integral. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two comparison maps `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `… 1`, i.e. a crossing of the two copies of the Igusa fibre, and write $\mathfrak X_O$ for the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$, assumed integral, and $x_n$ for the image of $n$ in $\mathfrak X_O$ under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔓.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` followed by `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. A ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` is given, subject to `hφO`, that $\varphi$ carries the germ at $x_n$ of the global section coming from $a \in O$ to the image of $a$ under the embedding $O \to \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)`, and, with the chart preimage nonempty, to `hφj`, that $\varphi$ carries the germ at the finite Igusa chart of each element of `chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` to its coefficient-embedded $q$-expansion. The place $w \in W$ (`hw`) is the one attached to $n$ by `𝔓.nodeEquiv` (`hn`). The chart presentation at $x_n$ consists of: `hsp₀` and `hsp₁`, the specialisations to $x_n$ of the images of the generic point of `fibre0` under the two comparison maps followed by `bcMap`; elements $u$, $v$, $w_0$ of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $x_n$ with $w_0$ a unit (`hw₀`); a natural number `width` with $uv = q^{\mathrm{width}} w_0$ (`huv`); `hmax`, the equality of the ideal $(q,u,v)$ with the maximal ideal of that stalk; and `h𝔭₀`, `h𝔭₁`, the equalities of $(q,u)$ and of $(q,v)$ with the contractions along the specialisation maps `stalkSpecializes hsp₀`, `stalkSpecializes hsp₁` of the respective maximal ideals, so $u$ and $v$ cut out the two branches.
--
--   Resolved model. $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ is a `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ q 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`: a proper flat integral locally Noetherian $O$-scheme $Y$ with a proper map `toDR` to $\mathfrak X_O$ over $O$, regular of stalk dimension at most two along the fibre over $q$, an isomorphism over the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, a finite set of nodes with widths at least one, an identification `nodeEquiv` of nodes with crossings, and a family `comp` of invertible ideal sheaves indexed by `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \sum_{x} \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(x) - 1)$ whose product is generated by $q$, with chosen generic points and further clauses. A node `nd` is given with `nodeEquiv nd = n` (`hnd`) and $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(nd) = \mathrm{width}$ (`hwidth`). The chart valuation law `hchartV` requires: for every section $t : \operatorname{Spec} O \to \mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.Y$ with $t$ followed by `𝔛reg.toBase` the identity, whose closed point is sent by $t$ followed by `toDR` to $x_n$, and every $d \in \mathbb N$ such that the additive valuation of $O$ of the image of $v$ (transported along the specialisation map) under `Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo` of $t$ followed by `toDR` equals $d$, and every component $c$, the closed point of $t$ lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp c` if and only if $c =$ `chainPos 𝔛reg.width nd d`, where `chainPos` is $\mathrm{inl}\,0$ for $d = 0$, $\mathrm{inr}\,(nd, d-1)$ for $0 < d < \mathrm{width}(nd)$, and $\mathrm{inl}\,1$ otherwise.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist an intermediate field $K_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, node coordinates $c_1 :$ `R.NodeCoordinates K₀ w` — that is, elements $x, y$ of the subring `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w` of those $f \in$ `R.nodeIntegers w` whose Laurent expansion lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N₀ * q) K₀`, satisfying `nodeResidue₁ w x = 0`, $\operatorname{ord}$ of `nodeResidue₂ w x` at `arithFrobC q κ N₀ • w` equal to $1$, `nodeResidue₂ w y = 0`, and $\operatorname{ord}_w$ of `nodeResidue₁ w y` equal to $1$ — and an element $u_0$ of `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w`, such that the following five assertions hold.
--
--   First, $u_0$ is a unit. Second, $c_1.x \cdot c_1.y = (\mathrm{nodeConst}_{K_0,w}(q))^{\mathrm{width}} \cdot u_0$, where $q$ is taken in `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K₀` $= A \cap K_0$ and `R.nodeConst K₀ w` is the constants homomorphism into `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w`. Third, $\varphi$ of the image of $u$ under the canonical map from the stalk at $x_n$ into the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ equals $c_1.x$, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)`. Fourth, the same with $v$ and $c_1.y$. Fifth, for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `P.reduceFst V = w` (that is, `P.sp` of the restriction of $V$ along $\bar\alpha$ equals $w$), such that $V$ is fixed by `arithmeticGalois (modularFunctionFieldFull (N₀ * q)) σ` for every $\sigma$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, for every section $t : \operatorname{Spec} O \to \mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.Y$ over $O$ such that $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the embedding $O \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ determined by `eO` and the inertia fixed field, followed by $t$, by `𝔛reg.toDR` and by `pullback.fst`, coincides with the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point `(𝔓.Meta.pointEquivPlace).symm V` followed by `𝔓.eeta` and `pullback.fst`, and for every $d \in \mathbb N$ with $c_1.\mathrm{yDepth}(V) = A.\mathrm{valuation}(q)^d$, where `yDepth V` is the $A$-valuation of the value of $c_1.y$ at $V$: for every component $c$ of `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`, the image under $t$ of the closed point of $O$ lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp c` if and only if $c =$ `chainPos 𝔛reg.width nd d`.
--
--   This is the dictionary statement at level $N_0q$ translating a chart presentation of one supersingular crossing on the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ into node coordinates on the prolongation side: the two branch parameters $u$, $v$ become coordinates $x$, $y$ with $xy = q^{\mathrm{width}}\cdot(\text{unit})$, and the component of the resolved model met by an $O$-section is read off from the $q$-adic depth of $y$ at the corresponding place. At this level the package orients the two copies of the Igusa fibre, so no swap parameter occurs. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_charts_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_charts_of_sp_eq_spPlace) and by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_width_eq_of_charts_of_sp_eq_spPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_width_eq_of_charts_of_sp_eq_spPlace).
